  "provenance_note": "Measurements below are the recorded output of the canonical cohort, produced by gpt-5.4-mini through the OpenAI adapter under rubric v1. Three things changed in the repository AFTER this cohort ran and are deliberately NOT retro-fitted into these numbers: (1) the per-rollout 'seed' field was a run label only -- never passed to the model API, never used to seed an RNG -- and has been removed from the harness; (2) rubric stage R0 was added, so run 11 scores 10 rather than 0; (3) rubric scores were rescaled to v2, mapping recorded 40 -> 30 and 75 -> 85 (0 -> 10 for run 11; 100 unchanged). No stage SET changes, so success_fraction and stage_completion_fraction are unaffected. Reports generated from now on carry generated_at_utc, git_commit, rubric_version and the agent configuration automatically. See reports/calibration-report.md for the full mapping table."
